Yes.  
Dosage: Low (1 week)

Explanation: Marva has ongoing expected acute postoperative pain on post-op day 3 after a major craniotomy, with exam findings consistent with normal incisional/scalp pain and documented inpatient opioid use every 6 hours. A short course of an immediate-release opioid is reasonable at discharge because non-opioid therapy alone appears insufficient. However, guidelines recommend limiting discharge opioid prescriptions to about 5–7 days in most postoperative patients, avoiding longer routine supplies, and providing a clear taper/weaning plan. Her opioid tolerance and chronic preoperative pain mean she may need some opioid coverage, but this surgery was not clearly pain-relieving, so a 4-week supply would be excessive;
